    "title": "Advanced Relative Clauses",
    "title_ko": "전치사 + 관계대명사",
    "focus_axis": "grammar"
  },
  "context": {
    "explanation_en": "In formal English, prepositions move before the relative pronoun instead of staying at the end of the clause: 'the person to whom I spoke' (formal) vs 'the person who I spoke to' (casual). This pattern is common in writing and formal speech.",
    "explanation_ko": "격식체 영어에서는 전치사가 절 끝에 남는 대신 관계대명사 앞으로 옵니다: 'the person to whom I spoke'(격식) vs 'the person who I spoke to'(캐주얼). 이 패턴은 글쓰기와 격식적인 말하기에서 흔합니다.",
    "key_expressions": [
      {
        "en": "The colleague with whom I worked has left.",
        "ko": "함께 일했던 동료가 떠났어요."
      },
      {
        "en": "This is the topic on which we disagree.",
        "ko": "이게 우리가 의견이 갈리는 주제예요."
      },
      {
        "en": "The company for which she works is expanding.",
        "ko": "그녀가 일하는 회사가 확장하고 있어요."
      }
    ]
  },
  "tasks": [
    {
